title: Volant Manticore Homa Framework C2 — Known 185.205.187.x Endpoints
id: b27c5d14-6a09-4f83-8e51-2c9d40f7ab63
status: experimental
description: Detects Windows network connections to the two command-and-control addresses Check Point Research attributed to Volant Manticore, an Iran-aligned espionage group linked to MOIS. Three Homa Framework stages were mapped to 185.205.187.109 on TCP/8000, and an earlier January 2026 Word lure reached 185.205.187.108 on TCP/25498. KuboShell registers hosts with MAC-derived files in C:\Users\Public and polls its IPFS command mailbox every 60 seconds.
references:
  - https://research.checkpoint.com/2026/volant-manticore-flying-under-the-radar/
  - https://malware.news/t/volant-manticore-flying-under-the-radar/127604#post_1
  - https://thehackernews.com/2026/11/iran-aligned-volant-manticore-uses-ipfs.html
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/11/25
tags:
  - attack.t1071
  - attack.t1102
  - attack.t1219
logsource:
  category: network_connection
  product: windows
detection:
  selection_dst_ip:
    DestinationIp:
      - '185.205.187.109'
      - '185.205.187.108'
  selection_dst_port:
    DestinationPort:
      - 8000
      - 25498
  condition: selection_dst_ip and selection_dst_port
falsepositives:
  - Unlikely — hardcoded actor-controlled VPS addresses on non-standard ports
level: high
